---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="Projects">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Projects</p>
    <h1>The tools around Virtual Lab.</h1>
    <p class="lead">A game for learning, visual components for teaching, and a numerical engine for the browser.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2 id="quantum-game">Quantum Game</h2>
    <p>A puzzle game with photons, polarization, superposition, and measurement. It provides a guided path into the same concepts and interface used by Virtual Lab.</p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="https://lab.quantumflytrap.com/game/">Play Quantum Game →</a></p>

    <h2 id="braketvue">BraKetVue</h2>
    <p>Open-source Vue components for visualizing complex quantum states and operators in bra–ket notation. Applicable to qubits, quantum chemistry, spin chains, and other discrete quantum systems.</p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Quantum-Game/bra-ket-vue">View BraKetVue on GitHub →</a></p>

    <h2 id="quantum-tensors">Quantum Tensors</h2>
    <p>An open-source TypeScript library for quantum information processing in the browser. It supports multipartite systems, qudits, basis changes, unitary operations, and measurements.</p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Quantum-Game/quantum-tensors">View Quantum Tensors on GitHub →</a></p>

    <h2 id="pulser-studio">Pulser Studio</h2>
    <p>A visual environment for designing pulse sequences for neutral-atom quantum computers, developed by Quantum Flytrap for Pasqal.</p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="https://pulserstudio.com/">Open Pulser Studio →</a></p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
